  message: "[REVIEW 2026-11-15: REAL TODAY, TEXT PARTLY STALE] 2026-11-15, dev e2b6ab8096, tree-sitter-agda 1.3.3: N.agda reproduces (ERROR 3:0-20:0; no `A`; `C` and `run` bare). The trigger is wider than an empty body. Empty nested module with nothing after its parent: correct symbols. Non-empty nested module (`c : Set / c = Set`): `c` named `A.c`, a following `run` loses `A`, a following top-level `module B` is named `A.C.B`. A nested record or two-constructor data inside a module makes the next sibling lose the module chain. Language pack 0.13.0 parses all 16 probes with `has_error=False`. agda.py:65-69 where claim still present; contradicted by W, W2, Cl. Fixtures: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/work/WI-molon. Full review: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/reports/WI-molon.md. No status or priority change made by this review."  # 8416
